><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">05</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Default deny</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">Each agent gets only the permissions its role needs, and I can pause or override any stage.</p></li><li style="border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px"><span style="font-family: var(--font-label); font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">06</span><h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--ink)">Knowledge lives with the code</h3><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; color: var(--text-muted)">The nearest CLAUDE.md wins. Humans write the guidance; agents read it before code.</p></li></ul>
